      "text": "We start with the expression \\(\\frac{(x + y)^2}{x^2 + y^2}\\). First, we expand the numerator:\n\\[\n(x + y)^2 = x^2 + 2xy + y^2.\n\\]\nThus, the expression becomes:\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2 + 2xy + y^2}{x^2 + y^2}.\n\\]\nWe can separate this into three fractions:\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2 + 2xy + y^2}{x^2 + y^2} = \\frac{x^2}{x^2 + y^2} + \\frac{2xy}{x^2 + y^2} + \\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2}.\n\\]\nThis can be rewritten as:\n\\[\n\\frac{x^2}{x^2 + y^2} + \\frac{2xy}{x^2 + y^2} + \\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2} = 1 + \\frac{2xy}{x^2 + y^2} + \\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2}.\n\\]\nNow, we need to find the minimum value of \\(\\frac{2xy}{x^2 + y^2} + \\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2}\\). To do this, we use the AM-GM inequality:\n\\[\n\\frac{2xy}{x^2 + y^2} + \\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2} = \\frac{2xy}{x^2 + y^2} + \\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2} \\geq 2\\sqrt{\\frac{2xy}{x^2 + y^2} \\cdot \\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2}} = 2\\sqrt{\\frac{2xy \\cdot y^2}{(x^2 + y^2)^2}} = 2\\sqrt{\\frac{2x^2y^2}{(x^2 + y^2)^2}} = 2\\sqrt{\\frac{2xy}{(x^2 + y^2)^2}}.\n\\]\nHowever, a simpler approach is to notice that by the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality in the form \\((a^2 + b^2)(c^2 + d^2) \\geq (ac + bd)^2\\):\n\\[\n(x^2 + y^2)\\left(\\frac{2xy}{x^2 + y^2} + \\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2}\\right) \\geq (x \\cdot \\sqrt{2xy} + y \\cdot y)^2 = (x\\sqrt{2xy} + y^2)^2.\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[\n(x^2 + y^2)(\\frac{2xy}{x^2 + y^2} + \\frac{y^2}{x^2 + y^2}) \\geq (x\\sqrt{2xy} + y^2)^2.\n\\]\nSo:\n\\[\n2xy + y^2 \\geq (x\\sqrt{2xy} + y^2)^2.\n\\]\nThe equality holds when \\(x = y\\). Substituting \\(x = y\\) into the original expression, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{(x + x)^2}{x^2 + x^2} = \\frac{(2x)^2}{2x^2} = \\frac{4x^2}{2x^2} = 2.\n\\]\nThus, the maximum value of \\(\\frac{(x + y)^2}{x^2 + y^2}\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
